    title: 'NRI Guide to Buying Property in India: Legal & Financial Steps',
    slug: 'nri-guide-buying-property-india',
    category: 'NRI',
    excerpt: 'A complete step-by-step guide for Non-Resident Indians (NRIs) looking to invest in the Indian real estate market, covering FEMA, taxation, and legalities.',
    content: `
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p>For millions of Non-Resident Indians (NRIs) scattered across the globe, owning a piece of India is more than just an investment — it is an emotional connection to their roots. In 2026, the Indian real estate market has matured significantly, offering a transparent, RERA-regulated environment that makes NRI property investment safer and more rewarding than ever before.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 mb-6">Who Can Buy Property in India as an NRI?</h2>
        <p>Under the Foreign Exchange Management Act (FEMA), an Indian citizen residing outside India (NRI) or an Overseas Citizen of India (OCI) can freely purchase residential and commercial property in India without special RBI approval. However, agricultural land and farmhouses are restricted.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 mb-6">Step-by-Step Process for NRI Property Purchase</h2>
        <h3 class="mt-8 mb-4">Step 1: Choose the Right Property</h3>
        <p>Start by identifying your goal — rental income, capital appreciation, or a future home? Delhi NCR offers all three. Areas like Gwal Pahari in Gurugram offer luxury floors with high appreciation, while Noida Expressway commercial spaces deliver rental yields above 8%.</p>

        <h3 class="mt-8 mb-4">Step 2: Verify Legal Titles (Due Diligence)</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li><strong>RERA Registration:</strong> Always check if the project is registered under RERA. Visit rera.up.gov.in for UP or hrera.org.in for Haryana.</li>
          <li><strong>Title Deed:</strong> Ensure the seller has a clear, marketable title with no encumbrances or disputes.</li>
          <li><strong>Approved Building Plan:</strong> Verify construction matches the sanctioned plan from local authority.</li>
          <li><strong>Encumbrance Certificate:</strong> Confirm no loans or legal charges are pending against the property.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-8 mb-4">Step 3: Financing Your Purchase</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li><strong>NRE Account:</strong> Funds are fully repatriable. Ideal for EMI payments.</li>
          <li><strong>NRO Account:</strong> For income earned in India. Repatriation limited to $1 million per financial year.</li>
          <li><strong>Home Loans:</strong> SBI, HDFC, ICICI offer NRI home loans at 8.5–9.5% per annum (2026 rates).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-12 mb-6">Tax Implications for NRIs</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li><strong>TDS on Purchase:</strong> Buyer deducts TDS at 20% when purchasing from an NRI seller.</li>
          <li><strong>Long-Term Capital Gains:</strong> Properties held 2+ years taxed at 20% with indexation benefits.</li>
          <li><strong>DTAA Benefits:</strong> India has DTAA with 90+ countries — avoid double taxation on your gains.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-12 mb-6">Power of Attorney (POA)</h2>
        <p>If you cannot be physically present for the transaction, grant a trusted representative a Power of Attorney, notarized in your country of residence and attested by the Indian Embassy or Consulate.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 mb-6">Repatriation of Funds</h2>
        <p>When selling the property, NRIs can repatriate the original investment amount. Capital gains, after applicable taxes, can also be repatriated through an NRO account.</p>

        <p class="my-8 p-4 bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-500 rounded-r-xl">Ready to invest in India? Our dedicated NRI desk at SS Realty provides end-to-end assistance — from property selection to home loan facilitation and registration. <a href="/contact-us" class="text-yellow-600 font-bold underline">Contact our NRI Desk today</a>.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 mb-6">Why Invest in Delhi NCR as an NRI?</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          <li>✅ Transparent RERA-regulated market</li>
          <li>✅ World-class infrastructure (metro, expressways, airports)</li>
          <li>✅ High rental demand from corporates and IT professionals</li>
          <li>✅ Rupee depreciation benefits for USD/GBP/AED earners</li>
          <li>✅ Emotional connection and future retirement planning</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    `,
